# User Profile — `<USER_FIRST_NAME>`

> Tier-2 persistent memory: identity, people, preferences, goals.
> Stable, slow-changing. If something here changes more than once a month,
> it belongs in MEMORY.md or the ledger, not here.
>
> **Where hermes actually reads this from (verified at hermes 0.21.0):**
> `HERMES_HOME/memories/USER.md`, which `deploy/start.sh` symlinks to the
> persistent disk — NOT `/root/.hermes/USER.md`, where the Dockerfile
> copies it. So the copy baked into the image is never in the system
> prompt; what the agent reads is whatever is on `/data/memories/`. The
> shipped Dockerfile leaves this as-is (fixing it changes agent behaviour).
> To make your USER.md live, copy it onto the disk once from the Render
> shell: `cp /root/.hermes/USER.md /root/.hermes/memories/USER.md`.
> Size it as if it loaded every turn regardless.

This is a **sanitised template**; the communication-style and tool-preference defaults below are one user's — edit them freely. Fill the placeholders in and save as
`USER.md` in this directory — the Dockerfile already COPYs that filename.
The real file is gitignored, so add it to your fork with
`git add -f hermes-config/USER.md` or the Render build fails at that COPY.

